summary:
I’m a professor and foresight expert who helps 𝐩𝐮𝐛𝐥𝐢𝐜 𝐥𝐞𝐚𝐝𝐞𝐫𝐬, 𝐜𝐨𝐫𝐩𝐨𝐫𝐚𝐭𝐞 𝐭𝐞𝐚𝐦𝐬, 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐬𝐭𝐮𝐝𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐬 𝐬𝐞𝐞 𝐛𝐞𝐲𝐨𝐧𝐝 𝐡𝐲𝐩𝐞 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐮𝐧𝐜𝐞𝐫𝐭𝐚𝐢𝐧𝐭𝐲 by showing them how to 𝐭𝐡𝐢𝐧𝐤 𝐝𝐢𝐟𝐟𝐞𝐫𝐞𝐧𝐭𝐥𝐲 𝐚𝐛𝐨𝐮𝐭 𝐭𝐡𝐞 𝐟𝐮𝐭𝐮𝐫𝐞 — without getting stuck in assumptions.

What motivates me is to help people build 𝐟𝐫𝐞𝐞𝐝𝐨𝐦 𝐨𝐟 𝐭𝐡𝐨𝐮𝐠𝐡𝐭 — by moving beyond narrow definitions of intelligence, strategies, progress, or the future. I love to build bridges between science and practice, technology and society, present and future generations. My work explores and develops solutions for responsible innovation and new modes of living and working in a technologized world.

During my studies, I discovered that I experience a strong kind of 𝐬𝐲𝐧𝐞𝐬𝐭𝐡𝐞𝐬𝐢𝐚 — an inborn ability to connect different senses and perceptions, such as seeing numbers in colors or time as a spatial landscape. This 𝐢𝐧𝐭𝐞𝐥𝐥𝐞𝐜𝐭𝐮𝐚𝐥 𝐚𝐦𝐛𝐢𝐝𝐞𝐱𝐭𝐞𝐫𝐢𝐭𝐲 helps me blend logic and emotion, intuition and evidence, and to identify patterns others often overlook.

What I offer (beyond being a professor - which I truly love):

// 𝐏𝐮𝐛𝐥𝐢𝐜 𝐬𝐩𝐞𝐚𝐤𝐢𝐧𝐠 on the future of technology and society
// 𝐅𝐨𝐫𝐞𝐬𝐢𝐠𝐡𝐭 𝐜𝐨𝐚𝐜𝐡𝐢𝐧𝐠 𝐚𝐧𝐝 𝐚𝐝𝐯𝐢𝐬𝐨𝐫𝐲 for leaders and teams
// 𝐒𝐞𝐫𝐢𝐨𝐮𝐬 𝐠𝐚𝐦𝐞𝐬 𝐝𝐞𝐯𝐞𝐥𝐨𝐩𝐦𝐞𝐧𝐭 for immersive learning experiences
// 𝐄𝐱𝐞𝐜𝐮𝐭𝐢𝐯𝐞 𝐞𝐝𝐮𝐜𝐚𝐭𝐢𝐨𝐧 in my fields of expertise
